parameters.content:
INPUT: { task_type, modality (text|vision|speech|document|code), sensitivity, max_cost }
OUTPUT: { provider, model, reason }
Decision order per blueprint Section 8: 1) can deterministic code do it - if so this router isn't called 2) can data leave Reeds env 3) modality 4) accuracy needed 5) cost/latency ceiling 6) provider health 7) needs second-model review.
Only OpenAI is currently configured (per Credential Register) - this router documents the decision even though there is only one real option today, so swapping in Claude/local later is a config change, not a rewrite.

parameters.jsCode:
const input = $json;
const sensitivity = input.sensitivity || 'business_confidential';

if (sensitivity === 'restricted' || sensitivity === 'secret') {
  return { provider: null, model: null, reason: 'Sensitivity too high for any currently configured external provider - route to Dominique for manual handling.', requires_approval: true };
}

// only OpenAI is configured today
let model = 'gpt-4o-mini';
if (input.task_type === 'complex_reasoning' || input.task_type === 'risk_assessment') {
  model = 'gpt-4o';
}
if (input.modality === 'vision') {
  model = 'gpt-4o';
}

return {
  provider: 'openai',
  model,
  reason: `Only OpenAI is configured/operational (Credential Register CR-002). Selected ${model} based on task_type='${input.task_type}', modality='${input.modality}'.`,
  requires_approval: false
};
